# LiveDisplay — one rule, and it is required.
#
# device.mk installs two LiveDisplay services:
#
#   vendor.lineage.livedisplay-service.sdm     display modes + picture adjustment
#   vendor.lineage.livedisplay-service.sysfs   outdoor mode (HBM)
#
# The SDM half needs nothing here. device/lineage/sepolicy/qcom/ already carries
# its domain, its exec label (file_contexts:2) and its vndbinder /
# display_vendor_data_file grants, and BOARD_VENDOR_SEPOLICY_DIRS picks that
# directory up through device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr/SEPolicy.mk.
#
# The sysfs half needs exactly one rule, for a reason that is easy to get wrong
# in both directions — see the long note on the two backlight entries in
# genfs_contexts.
#
# Upstream's policy (device/lineage/sepolicy/common/vendor/
# hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs.te:10) grants only
#
#     allow hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs sysfs_livedisplay_tuneable:file rw_file_perms;
#
# — a FILE rule and no :dir rule at all. That is sufficient upstream because the
# tuneables it labels all live under /devices/virtual/graphics/fb0/, whose parent
# directory stays plain `sysfs`, and every domain already has
# `allow domain sysfs:dir search` (system/sepolicy/private/domain.te:272).
#
# This device is DRM-only and has no fb0. Its HBM node is
# /devices/platform/soc/ae00000.qcom,mdss_mdp/backlight/panel0-backlight/hbm, and
# that parent directory cannot be left plain: recovery writes brightness in the
# same directory from the `init` domain, which is permitted only against
# vendor_sysfs_graphics (device/qcom/sepolicy_vndr/sm8750/generic/vendor/common/
# init.te:90-95, recovery_only) and can never be permitted against plain sysfs
# (private/init.te:862 neverallows `init sysfs:file { open write }`).
#
# So the parent is vendor_sysfs_graphics, and the traversal has to be granted
# explicitly — there is no blanket `sysfs_type:dir search` for arbitrary domains,
# only per-domain ones (apexd, priv_app, system_server, gmscore_app).
#
# Search only. The HAL opens exactly one file in that directory and has no reason
# to list it.
allow hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs vendor_sysfs_graphics:dir search;

# ⚠️ …and one more, because the genfscon split above DOES NOT TAKE EFFECT on this
# node. Measured on the running device (session 22):
#
#     ls -Z /sys/devices/platform/soc/ae00000.qcom,mdss_mdp/backlight/panel0-backlight/hbm
#       u:object_r:vendor_sysfs_graphics:s0        <- the PARENT's label
#
# i.e. hbm keeps the directory's type and never gets sysfs_livedisplay_tuneable,
# so the upstream rule that is supposed to cover it —
# device/lineage/sepolicy/common/vendor/hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs.te:10,
# `allow ... sysfs_livedisplay_tuneable:file rw_file_perms;` — never applies. The
# result today is one permissive AVC per boot; under enforcing it is a BOOT HANG,
# by exactly the mechanism OPEN-ISSUES #34 describes: SunlightEnhancement.cpp:42-53
# probes with access(path, R_OK|W_OK), that goes through inode_permission, the
# check fails, the constructor calls LOG(FATAL), the service never registers, and
# ISunlightEnhancement is declared in the VINTF manifest.
#
#     avc: denied { write } for comm="vendor.lineage." name="hbm"
#          scontext=u:r:hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs:s0
#          tcontext=u:object_r:vendor_sysfs_graphics:s0 tclass=file permissive=1
#
# ★ This is NOT the usual "the entry is missing" or "the path is wrong". All four
# things you would check are correct, and each was checked:
#
#   1. Both genfscon lines survive into the policy the KERNEL loaded — dumped
#      with `adb pull /sys/fs/selinux/policy` + `checkpolicy -b -M -C`, not read
#      out of the source.
#   2. The path is right: the parent entry matches the same inode (ino 142804,
#      the one the AVC names), which it could only do by prefix-matching that
#      exact path.
#   3. The type exists and is in both the fs_type and sysfs_type attribute sets.
#   4. Longest-prefix genfscon works fine on this device. Every genfscon entry in
#      the loaded policy that is strictly longer than another entry that is its
#      prefix, and whose path exists on the hardware, was checked live: 190 of
#      198 child entries WIN, including this file's own soc:lenovo_kb /
#      soc:lenovo_kb/wakeup pair. The other 7 are artefacts of the comparison
#      (trailing-slash entries and /sys/class symlinks). hbm is the single
#      genuine failure on the whole device.
#
# `chcon` on the node succeeds and sticks, so kernfs is not refusing the label —
# whatever this is, it is between the kernel's genfs lookup and this one inode,
# and it was not worth more of flash-2's budget to chase. What matters is that
# the tree must not DEPEND on that entry.
#
# So: grant the write against the type the node actually has. The genfscon line
# stays — it is correct, it costs nothing, and if the anomaly ever resolves the
# node lands on the narrower type with no further change.
#
# Cost of the widening, stated plainly: this domain can now read and write every
# vendor_sysfs_graphics file, which on this device includes
# panel0-backlight/brightness and the sde/drm attributes under
# ae00000.qcom,mdss_mdp. That is a display HAL being given display sysfs; it is
# not nothing, and it is the smallest rule that makes Outdoor mode work under
# enforcing.
allow hal_lineage_livedisplay_sysfs vendor_sysfs_graphics:file rw_file_perms;
